### ========== EXERCISE 5: Enrollment API Tests ==========

### 1. GET all enrollments (should return empty array [])
GET http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments

### 2. POST create a new enrollment (should return 201 with Location header)
POST http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S-001",
  "courseCode": "CS-101"
}

### 3. GET specific enrollment (replace {id} with actual ID from POST response)
GET http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments/{id}

### 4. DELETE enrollment (replace {id} with actual ID)
DELETE http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments/{id}

### 5. DELETE same ID again (should return 404)
DELETE http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments/nonexistent-id

### 6. Duplicate enrollment (should log Warning)
POST http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S-001",
  "courseCode": "CS-101"
}

### ========== EXERCISE 6: ProblemDetails Tests ==========

### 7. Error endpoint (should return ProblemDetails JSON)
GET http://localhost:5003/api/error

### 8. Non-existent enrollment (should return 404 ProblemDetails)
GET http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments/nonexistent-id

### ========== SESSION 1: Protected Endpoint Tests ==========

### 9. Anonymous access (should return 401)
GET http://localhost:5003/api/assessments/results

### 10. Authenticated access (should return 200)
GET http://localhost:5003/api/assessments/results
X-Training-User: test-student

### ========== EXERCISE 2: Worker Test ==========

### 11. Worker smoke test
GET http://localhost:5003/api/enrollments/worker-smoke